Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?perf=20phase=2011=20patch=200130=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?wave-34=20backdrop=20sub-region=20partial=20blit?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reduce backdrop-blit bandwidth by skipping screen-Y rows where the
FG/BG tilemap will fully overdraw the backdrop. Targets the dominant
4 ms / flip cache→window or tile-loop transfer on PODP83+Cirrus per
`wave_19_path_b_dead.md` 17 MB/s sysmem measurement.

Mechanism. At map_flush_graphics (called on every map change), walk
map.tiles[x][y] once and build the per-row `g_bg_visible_per_row` bool
table. Row y is "backdrop-visible" iff at least one column has
map.tiles[col][y] == 0 (the "empty tile" Cave Story convention =
nothing drawn = backdrop pixel reaches the composited framebuffer).
Rows with ALL non-zero tiles are assumed fully FG-opaque (no backdrop
pixels need to land there). One ~76,800-compare scan per map load is
trivial vs the per-frame savings.

Per-frame, `_compute_bg_visible_yrange` walks the visible map rows
from camera_y and projects to screen-Y, returning the (top, bot)
inclusive range covering all backdrop-visible rows. The range is
cached on (curmap, mapy_tile_origin) so recompute fires only when the
camera crosses a TILE_H boundary — a few times per second in normal
play, not per-frame. The cache-miss counter
g_bg_visible_y_recomputes_block is exposed in flush-instr's audit
emit for verification.

Dispatch in map_draw_backdrop's cacheable-scrolltype branch
(BK_PARALLAX / BK_FOLLOWFG / BK_FASTLEFT / BK_FIXED). When
`bg_subregion_active()` returns true (default; killswitch
`SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BG_SUBREGION_BLIT=0` reverts) AND the computed
range is a proper subset of [0, screenHeight-1]:

- HIT path: `r->drawCachedBackdropClipped(cache, bg_top, bg_bot)`
  (new Renderer method) — SDL_BlitSurface with clipped src/dst rects.
  Saves (1 - (bg_bot - bg_top + 1)/screenHeight) of the full transfer.
- THRASHING tile loop (patch 0126 wave-30): outer Y loop bails on
  iterations whose dst-Y is entirely outside [bg_top, bg_bot]. Edge
  tiles that straddle the boundary blit fully (no src-rect trim);
  ~6.7% over-blit worst case per edge, preserved for simplicity.
- WARM miss cache-fill path is INTENTIONALLY UNCHANGED — the cache
  surface must stay full-screen so subsequent HIT frames have valid
  content as visible-Y range changes. Optimizing only the dominant
  path (HIT + THRASHING) keeps cache correctness intact.

Out of scope. BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS / BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS_NOFALLLEFT
(Outer Wall / Balcony / title menu) use a separate render path
(`_render_layered_to_surface` with 5 layers + clear-color);
sub-region clip on that path is a possible future slot but the layer
compositing semantics need separate analysis. BK_HIDE / BK_HIDE2 /
BK_HIDE3 early-return without a backdrop blit, so they're already
optimal.

Conservative correctness model. The "tile_id == 0" proxy assumes any
non-zero tile is fully FG-opaque. False negatives are possible only
if a non-zero tile contains transparent pixels AND that tile is in a
row where ALL other columns are also non-zero — would manifest as
"leftover framebuffer junk shows through a transparent edge of a
terrain tile" caught by build-qa visual smoke. Killswitch reverts to
the bit-for-bit pre-patch behavior.

Architectural classification. CPU-cheap, bandwidth-bound win — fewer
INDEX8 bytes transferred per flip. Distinct from the wave-31 Lever B
trap (parked at `patches/nxengine-evo/_disabled/0127-*.patch`) which
re-introduced cache→window bandwidth equal to the underlying tile-
render bandwidth. Slot 0130 ELIMINATES bytes-transferred for FG-
opaque rows, which is what the 17 MB/s sysmem bandwidth math actually
rewards. Composes additively with patch 0126 (wave-30 thrashing-
detect): the THRASHING path's tile loop now also skips outer-loop
iterations for clipped rows, stacking the savings.

Predicted savings. -1.5 to -3 ms / flip on Mimiga Village heavy-music
(upper ~50% of screen is sky-only per visual inspection → ~50%
bandwidth savings × ~4 ms full-blit cost ≈ ~2 ms). Per
`perf_predictions_unreliable.md` predictions historically wrong 5-30×
on real HW; wave-34 PODP-83 measurement is the essential gate.

Instrumentation. 5 per-block counters in NXE::Diag (storage +
externs):

- g_bg_subregion_clip_top_block / g_bg_subregion_clip_bot_block:
  Sample-readout of the most-recent flip's visible-Y range. Will vary
  frame-to-frame as camera scrolls — the data-driven discriminator
  for option-(A) implementation vs static-LUT alternatives.
- g_bg_subregion_engaged_count_block / g_bg_subregion_fallback_count_block:
  Per-block running counts of "optimization fired" vs "fell back to
  full blit". Sum should be ~100 per block when killswitch is on.
- g_bg_visible_y_recomputes_block: How often the per-tile-Y cache
  missed in the block. Sanity-check sanity should be small.

Emit line `[bg-subregion n=100 clip_top=N clip_bot=N engaged=N
fallback=N recomputes=N]` gated on SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLIP_INSTR=1
(same gate as flip-stat / flip-body-stat per flush-instr's contract).
Default-on for the optimization itself, but counters silent unless
FLIP_INSTR is also enabled. Counter equation
`engaged + fallback ≈ 100` holds when subregion-blit is on across
the block.

Smoke. Builds clean at i486 -O3 -funroll-loops. New strings in
binary: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BG_SUBREGION_BLIT env-var symbol,
drawCachedBackdropClipped function symbol, [bg-subregion ...] emit
template. All prior slot markers (TILE_BOUNDS_SKIP slot 0128,
snd-shutdown[3.5/6] slot 0129, thrashing-detect engaged slot 0126)
retained. Slot 0127 Lever B markers still absent (wave-32 revert
intact). Real-HW gate: wave-34 W34A1 (default-on, BG_SUBREGION_BLIT
unset) vs W34A2 (BG_SUBREGION_BLIT=0 control) on Mimiga Village heavy-
music — flush-instr's contract uses the engaged/fallback discriminator
to confirm mechanism engagement before attributing the fps delta.

Files. New: src/graphics/Renderer.cpp drawCachedBackdropClipped()
method + _abl_bg_subregion() env-helper + 5 counter storage + audit
emit; src/graphics/Renderer.h drawCachedBackdropClipped() decl;
src/Utils/diagnostic_timers.h 5 counter externs + bg_subregion_active()
forward-decl; src/map.cpp _build_bg_visible_table() +
_compute_bg_visible_yrange() helpers + cache-state statics + dispatch
in map_draw_backdrop + hook in _backdrop_cache_reset for map-change
invalidation. ~250 LOC including comments (the brief said ~100 LOC;
overage is mostly the documented counter infrastructure flush-instr
spec'd in Q2 of the design-coordination DM, plus the visibility-table
helpers which the brief implicitly assumed).
